    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="1135" n="1015" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-15T11:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:54
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Reference to my despatch of February 25th. Request Department’s instruction
                    as to whether I am to take up with Mr. Dwight W. Morrow<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d833-f1"/> who arrives tomorrow from Panama the scheme for an
                    examination and statement of the national finances and system of public <pb
                        facs="1136" n="1016" xml:id="pg1016"/> accounting outlined in said despatch.
                    In this connection see my despatch March 9th enclosure number 2.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d833-f2"/> Charges in Congress and in public press persist that the
                    national expenditures are not within the readjusted budget and the Government
                    seems unable produce convincing proof that they are. It is likewise true that no
                    national audit and statement prepared by the Cuban Government will command
                    confidence either here or in the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
